  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Clinic Map",
    "overview": "Each screen is a guide map. One flat field of leaf green, the **land**, leads the screen and holds its one key fact: a greeting, a screen's title, the app's own line on the account screens. Its edge is a softly swelling **coastline**, never a straight card edge. Everything else sits on the **ground**, a pale sage water in light and a deep green-black in dark. The reader should know in under a second what needs them now, in glare, on a budget phone, with little practice with software.\n\nControls are **capsules**. A primary capsule is green with a round ink **chip** riding its trailing edge; when the thing is live the chip crosses to the leading edge, so the chip's place repeats what the label says. Coral is kept for attention only: an allergy, an amount owed, an ended plan, an action that cannot be undone. The page is flat. Depth appears only on what floats over it in the top layer: sheets, cards, popovers.\n\nThe world refuses the category's white-cards-and-pastel-icon-tiles grid, and cold grey ERP tables. It has no photographs or illustrations; people are initials.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "The land leads every signed-in screen and every account screen; its edge is an authored coastline.",
      "Ground and surface carry everything else; menus are one list on the ground, parted by hairlines.",
      "Capsule controls with a travelling chip; everything you tap is round-ended and at least 44 px.",
      "Green, ink and one coral. No yellow, gold, blue or lilac.",
      "Figtree in two weights; display numerals big, bold and tight.",
      "One duration (`--duration-map`) and one curve (`--ease-map`), no overshoot; instant under reduced motion.",
      "Light and dark ship together; every text pair is held to WCAG AA by `tests/contract/design-tokens.test.ts`."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Coral Is Attention Rule",
        "body": "Coral marks only what must not be missed: an allergy, money owed or to bill, an ended plan or view-only clinic, no connection, an error, an action that cannot be undone. A required-field asterisk is muted, not coral. If a screen's coral is not one of these, remove it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Gold Rule",
        "body": "No yellow, gold, blue or lilac anywhere, in either theme (the user's fixed constraint). Warnings use coral and their words, not amber.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "Every state that has a colour also has words and an icon or a position: the status pill carries a dot and its word, the band carries its icon and sentence, the capsule's chip changes side. The tone of a status comes from `src/constants/statuses.ts` (`neutral`, `live`, `attention`), never from the screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Weights Rule",
        "body": "Regular (400) and bold (700) only. Hierarchy comes from size and weight, never from a third weight, italics or capitals. No uppercase labels, no letter-spaced kickers.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tight Numeral Rule",
        "body": "Numbers that matter (tokens, rupees, counts) are bold, at token size or larger, line-height 0.95, slightly negative tracking, and `tabular-nums`. Any amount, time, phone number or date in a row or field is `tabular-nums`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sixteen Pixel Floor",
        "body": "Inputs never fall below 16 px (`font-size: max(1rem, 1em)` in the base layer) so iOS does not zoom.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Centre Plus Rule",
        "body": "On a phone the ＋ is the middle of the bottom bar, a 60 px land chip raised out of its top edge and ringed with ground. It is never moved, hidden by a missing neighbour, or replaced by a floating button. On tablet and desktop the same Quick Actions open from the rail's round ＋ and the sidebar's **Add** (D69).",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Land Leads Rule",
        "body": "A signed-in screen begins with its land (`CoastHeader` holding `PageHeader`), after any band. Its title lives on the land; there is no separate top bar.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Raised Only In The Top Layer Rule",
        "body": "A shadow means \"this floats over the page and will go away\". Rows, fields, stat tiles, the land and the shell never cast one. A surface row is set apart by its fill on the ground, an outline row by a `--line` ring.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Capsule Rule",
        "body": "If a person can tap it or type in it, it is round-ended. Square corners and small radii do not appear on controls.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Whole Screen Rule",
        "body": "A screenshot sits whole in its lake, inset (`rounded-row`) so its corners clear the lake's curve: the lake's proportion and the screen's width are set together (`FRAMES`), never by cropping the screen to fit.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Coastline Edge Rule",
        "body": "Land ends in a coastline from `COASTLINES`, never in a straight edge or a card radius, and never in a path generated at render time. Only the `Pin` sits on the coastline; no other text crosses it.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** start every signed-in screen with its land (`CoastHeader` + `PageHeader`), and every account screen with `AuthScene`.",
      "**Do** use `Button` for every button and pick the variant by meaning: one `primary` per view, `danger` only for the irreversible, `secondary` beside a primary, `quiet` for the way out.",
      "**Do** list menus (Settings, My account, More) as `RowList look=\"menu\"` with `Row look=\"menu\"` and a bare `RowIcon` (D75); use `surface` rows for people and records, `quiet` rows for records not yet in play.",
      "**Do** name colours, sizes, radii and the shadow only by their tokens (`bg-land`, `text-title`, `rounded-row`, `shadow-raised`).",
      "**Do** put every create or edit form in a `Sheet`, every outcome through `useResponse()`, and every irreversible action behind a confirm card.",
      "**Do** set money, times, tokens and phone numbers in `tabular-nums`, and the numbers that matter at token or display size.",
      "**Do** check every screen in light and dark, at phone, tablet and desktop, with no axe violations.",
      "**Do** keep every target at least 44 px and every input at 16 px or more.",
      "**Do** show the app outside itself only as real screenshots, in light and dark, whole in a `ShotLake`, the theme's own shown by `.for-light` / `.for-dark` (D400, D401)."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use yellow, gold, blue or lilac, in either theme.",
      "**Don't** use coral for anything that is not attention (allergy, owed or to bill, ended plan, offline, error, irreversible).",
      "**Don't** let colour carry a state alone; add its word and its icon or chip position.",
      "**Don't** give a menu row its own card, or set an icon on a tile, tinted square or circle under it (§32.1 Refuses, D75).",
      "**Don't** build the white-cards-and-pastel-icon-tiles dashboard grid or a grey ERP table.",
      "**Don't** end land in a straight edge, draw a coastline at render time, or let text other than the `Pin` cross a coastline.",
      "**Don't** put a shadow on anything that sits on the page; `--shadow-raised` is for the top layer only, and for a screenshot in a landing lake.",
      "**Don't** add a third font weight, uppercase or letter-spaced labels, or eyebrows above titles.",
      "**Don't** use the browser's native select, date or time pickers (D65).",
      "**Don't** add a top bar on a phone, move the ＋ off the centre of the bottom bar, or replace it with a floating button.",
      "**Don't** add photographs or illustrations; people are initials (`Avatar`).",
      "**Don't** crop a screenshot to fit a lake, or put the landing's screens on feature cards or beside a split hero (D400).",
      "**Don't** use bounce, spring or overshoot, or a second duration or curve."
    ]
  }
}
